{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T17:19:58.197Z","ordinal":36453,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a08c55-56f5-7b22-b7f9-a59ff9d5ccf5","author":"/root/simple_review_storage","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/simple_review_storage\nPayload:\nCurrent storage/TUI findings:\n\n- `internal/cli/distill_quality_adjudicate_tui_v1.go:41-54` builds `byViewID` and passes `func(itemID, admission, authority, safety, rationale string)`. The callback resolves the item and calls `session.save(...)`.\n- `distillQualityAdjudicationSessionV1.save` (`distill_quality_adjudicate_v1.go:207`) constructs `distillQualityHumanAdjudicationV1`, validates it, rejects duplicate `PacketID`, atomically rewrites the reviewer’s JSONL, then increments `Reviewed`/decrements `Remaining`.\n- Resume already works: `openDistillQualityAdjudicationSessionV1` loads `human/<adjudicator>.jsonl`, indexes reviewed packet IDs, and `buildDistillQualityAdjudicateItemsV1` excludes them.\n- Storage is per-adjudicator JSONL, mode `0600`, sorted by packet ID. This is the right persistence boundary to retain.\n\nCurrent human schema (`distill_quality_panel_v1.go:169-185`) stores:\n\n- packet/digest bindings and advisory aggregate digest;\n- `Decision`: `accept | reject | needs_review`;\n- six-dimensional `Dimensions` proof labels;\n- rationale, reviewer, timestamp.\n\nValidation (`:585-633`) requires all identity/digest fields, a valid old `Decision`, and 1–12 unique dimensions. The current three TUI answers map through `makeDistillQualityHumanAdjudicationV1` (`distill_quality_adjudicate_v1.go:729`): admission determines `Decision`; authority/safety become proof labels; the other dimensions are `not_applicable`.\n\nThe smallest backward-compatible representation is additive: retain the existing v1 fields and add an explicit optional field such as:\n\n```go\nAgreement string `json:\"agreement,omitempty\"` // \"agree\" or \"disagree\"\n```\n\nNew TUI saves should populate `Agreement`; old records with an empty field remain readable. Do not encode agreement by abusing `Decision`/admission—the latter means “should this item be admitted,” while the requested question is whether the human agrees with the judges. If only agree/disagree is wanted, use an enum with exactly those values; no need for `unclear` unless desired later.\n\nTo make minimal records possible, either:\n\n1. keep writing the legacy decision/dimensions alongside `Agreement` (smallest code/schema change), or\n2. introduce a v2 human record schema if the old fields are to be removed. Because strict JSON decoding is used, removing them is not backward-compatible.\n\nRequired code changes for the simplified flow:\n\n- `internal/tui/quality_review.go`\n  - Replace the three-stage `QualityReviewDecision` (`Admission`, `Authority`, `Safety`) with one agreement answer.\n  - Change `QualityReviewSaveFunc` or add a new callback accepting `(itemID, agreement, rationale)`.\n  - Simplify stages/prompts/confirmation in `Update`, `stageName`, `stagePrompt`, `decisionView`, and `choiceSummary`.\n  - Remove the visible queue pane: `View` currently calls `queueView` at lines ~481–490; `queueView` is ~540–590. `resize` currently reserves a 38-column queue pane for wide terminals.\n  - Keep the existing explicit-confirm save behavior and result counters.\n\n- `internal/cli/distill_quality_adjudicate_tui_v1.go`\n  - Adapt the callback to save the new agreement field.\n  - `makeDistillQualityReviewItemV1` currently appends unavailable judges as synthetic `State: \"missing\"` rows at lines ~139–142. Omit those rows entirely; `Aggregate.MissingJudges` can remain in storage/report metadata.\n  - Continue mapping judge verdicts to readable summaries/rationales.\n\n- `internal/cli/distill_quality_panel_v1.go`\n  - Add the additive `Agreement` field and validate `\"\"` (legacy) or `agree`/`disagree`.\n  - Add a helper such as `makeDistillQualityHumanAgreementV1`.\n  - Keep current digest validation so a saved answer is still bound to the exact packet and advisory panel.\n\n- `internal/cli/distill_quality_adjudicate_v1.go`\n  - Update `session.save` and the constructor. Duplicate-packet rejection and atomic JSONL persistence already provide resume semantics.\n  - Add a query/helper for disagreement, e.g. `loadAllDistillQualityHumanAdjudicationsV1`, because current loading requires a specific adjudicator ID.\n\nReporting currently does not consume human decisions at all. `renderDistillQualityHumanReviewV1` (`distill_quality_report_v1.go:19`) only loads packets/judges and writes aggregates, `human-review.md`, audit markdown, and a blank template. Therefore disagreed items are not currently reportable. Add a human-decision section/artifact by scanning `human/*.jsonl`, loading each reviewer file with existing validation, and filtering `Agreement == \"disagree\"` (ideally include packet ID, reviewer, statement, filter result, judge summaries, and rationale). Keep the existing audit output unchanged if desired and add a concise “human disagreements” report.\n\nTests needing updates/additions:\n\n- `internal/tui/quality_review_test.go`\n  - Replace three-answer save assertions with one agree/disagree answer.\n  - Remove queue-pane expectations (`queueView`, wide layout); assert statement/filter/judges/confirmation remain visible.\n  - Add unavailable judges omitted from rendered view.\n  - Retain tests for explicit confirmation, save failure retaining the item, skip/quit, resume-compatible callback behavior.\n\n- `internal/cli/distill_quality_adjudicate_v1_test.go`\n  - Update input sequences and expected records.\n  - Assert `Agreement` persists and a second invocation skips the reviewed packet without changing the file.\n  - Add a disagree record and query/report assertion.\n\n- `internal/cli/distill_quality_panel_v1_test.go`\n  - Add validation tests for `agree`, `disagree`, invalid values, and legacy empty agreement.\n\n- `internal/cli/distill_quality_report_v1_test.go`\n  - Seed `human/<reviewer>.jsonl`; assert generated reporting exposes only disagreement records as actionable results.\n  - Preserve the existing blank-template and missing-judge tests.\n\nQueue selection (`--queue calibration|critical|...`) can remain as a backend attention-routing feature; only the visual queue list needs removal."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08c52-627e-72c2-ad24-e4d4de487a71"}}}
