{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T17:58:58.700Z","ordinal":37127,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a08c79-0d8c-7f73-9c4c-9fc79f4388df","author":"/root/phase2_delta_path","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/phase2_delta_path\nPayload:\nFindings:\n\n- The current resume path only resumes inside one sealed bundle. `judge` loads the current packet map and resumes by `PacketID`; `loadDistillQualityJudgeVerdictsV1` rejects unknown packet IDs or any packet/item/prompt/payload digest mismatch.\n- Human resume is stricter: `loadDistillQualityHumanAdjudicationsV1` rejects old records that reference packets absent from the new bundle. It validates packet digests and `AdvisoryDigest`, so copying the existing 29-line file wholesale is unsafe.\n- `report` always renders the full current run. There is no parent-run, reuse, changed-packet, or delta concept.\n- Therefore existing resume cannot perform a selector rebase safely without code changes. An external `jq` filtering script could approximate it for this run, but it would not handle unavailable judges or persist the reuse boundary reproducibly.\n\nCurrent sealed run:\n\n```text\n/Users/thomi/.local/share/entire/evals/phase2/quality-run-v1-33808625\n```\n\nIt has 719 verdict lines for each of Copilot, Cursor, and Claude, and 29 human records in:\n\n```text\nhuman/ashtom.jsonl\n```\n\nThe human file must be migrated by exact packet identity, never by source/session/turn/text. A record is reusable only when the new packet matches the old packet byte-for-byte/canonically, including:\n\n```text\npacket_id\npacket_digest\nitem_digest\nprompt_digest\npayload_digest\n```\n\nThe old and new advisory aggregate must also have the same `advisory_digest`. Changed selector results—including an admitted item becoming filtered—must lose their old human label.\n\nSmallest durable implementation:\n\n1. Add a reuse/base-bundle input to preparation or a dedicated `rebase` operation.\n\n2. Compare old/new packets canonically. Copy old judge verdicts only for exact matches, and record explicit “unavailable in base” markers for exact packets where a judge had no usable verdict. Do not synthesize invalid verdicts.\n\n3. Update the judge runner’s pending calculation so:\n   - exact packets with copied verdicts are skipped;\n   - exact packets explicitly unavailable in the base are skipped and remain `MissingJudges`;\n   - only new/changed packets go to providers;\n   - model identity must match before reusing a verdict.\n\n4. Migrate human records only when all packet digests and the advisory digest match. Drop changed/stale records silently into the delta set rather than making the new bundle unloadable. Regenerate `RecordID` for the new run while retaining the decision, rationale, and timestamp.\n\n5. Emit `human-review-delta.md` containing only new/changed/unmigrated packets, and add a `delta` adjudication queue that presents exactly those packets. Existing records then remain skipped automatically.\n\nIntended command flow:\n\n```sh\nentire brain facts distill-quality prepare \\\n  --out \"$NEW\" \\\n  --reuse-from /Users/thomi/.local/share/entire/evals/phase2/quality-run-v1-33808625\n\nentire brain facts distill-quality judge --bundle \"$NEW\" --judge copilot\nentire brain facts distill-quality judge --bundle \"$NEW\" --judge cursor\nentire brain facts distill-quality judge --bundle \"$NEW\" --judge claude\n\nentire brain facts distill-quality report --bundle \"$NEW\"\n\nentire brain facts distill-quality adjudicate \\\n  --bundle \"$NEW\" \\\n  --adjudicator ashtom \\\n  --queue delta \\\n  --limit 100\n```\n\nLikely files:\n\n- `internal/cli/facts_distill_quality_cmd_v1.go`: flags/rebase orchestration\n- `internal/cli/distill_quality_judge_runner_v1.go`: exact-match reuse and pending filtering\n- `internal/cli/distill_quality_run_io_v1.go`: reuse/skip artifact loading and validation\n- `internal/cli/distill_quality_adjudicate_v1.go`: safe human-record migration and `delta` queue\n- `internal/cli/distill_quality_report_v1.go`: compact delta report\n\nTests should cover exact-vs-same-ID/different-digest packets, unavailable base judges remaining missing, provider invocation only for changed packets, stale human records being excluded rather than applied, and delta adjudication containing no already-reviewed packet."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08c74-fa42-7203-94f4-192afac6c9d7"}}}
