{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:12:05.200Z","ordinal":37416,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a08c85-0dcf-7913-b145-e0f83eb2eb8d","call_id":"call_Jo1XGSoy8TeHuxyA6uXQEUrs","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/phase2_delta_impl\",\"agent_status\":\"interrupted\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/phase2_label_analysis\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only audit complete.\\n\\nFor the 20 new records, the six clear selector false positives (candidate admitted, with a judge majority of `should_admit=no`) are:\\n\\n- `05488f0a` — “Implement the whole plan. Test and verify…”; one-off execution directive.\\n- `05c7e254` — long `GOAL`/SNAP20 benchmark campaign; task plan/pasted context.\\n- `08dc5b54` — “Review Entire trails 3, 6, and 10… make sure… mergable”; one-off work order.\\n- `d2f46e65` — benchmark result followed by “make a concrete Sonnet plan”; one-off planning.\\n- `e43fa083` — “Yes” accepting a bugbot rerun; session-local action.\\n- `ee0d466a` — “implement it now… audit… make PR”; one-off execution directive.\\n\\nThe retained human disagreement is `0547e5dc`: the “clean slate / choose best stuff / ignore README numbers for now” preference. Copilot and Cursor rejected admission; Claude was uncertain. The human accepted it. This is a valid admission-for-inspection example, but not necessarily a durable-memory fact.\\n\\nTwo additional admitted records (`d3bb8aa1`, `e361bf98`) had no judge majority, so they should remain ambiguity fixtures rather than be counted among the six consensus false positives.\\n\\nThe proposed admission-versus-final-memory distinction matches the durable-facts plan’s quality gate: durable, useful, non-discoverable, resolved knowledge only; plans, one-off instructions, and pasted material are excluded. However, the current Phase 2 judge prompt uses “admission” in that same final-durability sense, so the distinction is not yet encoded contractually.\\n\\nCritical risk: loosening admission for recall without a separate explicit durability/write gate will let these six directive/plan false positives reach durable memory. Preserve all six as rejection regressions, `0547e5dc` as the human-approved disagreement fixture, and `d3bb8aa1`/`e361bf98` as no-majority ambiguity fixtures.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/phase2_selector_calibration\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Implemented selector calibration changes, uncommitted.\\n\\n- Suppresses current-run task/runbook cases and bare `Yes` operational approvals.\\n- Keeps durable rules, explicit temporal constraints, project-goal `I want…`, revisions, and closed negatives eligible.\\n- Bumped candidate schema version to 3.\\n- Added table-driven sanitized regression coverage.\\n\\nFocused admission tests and diff checks pass. Quality impact: fewer false-positive provider calls with only bounded precompiled-regex overhead per candidate turn.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08c74-fa42-7203-94f4-192afac6c9d7"}}}
