{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:12:57.632Z","ordinal":38210,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0200a-63d8-7b21-adef-c3850aecebf7","turn_id":"01a08cbc-3e2e-71d0-bf78-c2587ebbc22c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-19629d35-abbc-4e68-8bba-dd07ddc06fdc","process_id":"81191","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n '^#{1,6} |Status:|Exit gate|exit gate|Phase [0-9]|pending|remain|remaining|defer|block|default|promotion|human|paired|retrieval|relationship|quality|call|cache' docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n '^#{1,6} |Status:|Exit gate|exit gate|Phase [0-9]|pending|remain|remaining|defer|block|default|promotion|human|paired|retrieval|relationship|quality|call|cache' docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md","query":"^#{1,6} |Status:|Exit gate|exit gate|Phase [0-9]|pending|remain|remaining|defer|block|default|promotion|human|paired|retrieval|relationship|quality|call|cache","path":"candidate_distillation_plan.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"1:# Candidate-First Distillation Plan\n3:Status: Phase 3 conservative-write exit gate complete. Phase 2 has a sealed\n4:advisory multi-model pre-adjudication package, a resumable human review\n6:human-labeled audit, paired fact-quality runs, and retrieval gates remain\n7:pending and block default promotion (2026-09-10).\n11:direct-user candidate cards, one card per extraction call, conservative exact\n12:upserts with no reconciliation-agent call, separate rollback-safe session-cache\n14:Legacy remains the default.\n16:The Phase 2 branch adds candidate-id-framed multi-card output, deterministic\n18:a bounded success-only member cache, one-level failure bisection, provider usage\n20:taxonomy, the legacy cache, and the manifest unchanged. Exclude/purge resets the\n21:derived member cache; privacy verification, atomic-temp cleanup, and publish\n28:The Phase 3A branch routes opt-in non-shadow candidate runs through that same\n29:framed, packed, member-cached extraction path. It materializes only exact fact\n37:artifact. Different fact ids remain separate with no automatic merge or\n40:Phase 3B adds that evidence-bearing shape without changing reconciliation. A\n47:`facts/distill-v2/relationships.ndjson` and is exposed only through the\n48:read-only `facts relationships list` command. It has no action, confidence,\n50:publication path. Executable merge/supersede proposals remain unchanged and\n61:fail merely because a subject is broad. It indexes exact subject blocks, sorts\n62:them deterministically, and admits a block only when its complete pair set fits\n63:the remaining 4,096-entry and 4 MiB store budgets. A 91-member block (4,095\n64:pairs) is admissible; a 92-member block (4,186 pairs) is skipped before pair\n65:enumeration. Byte- or capacity-limited blocks are likewise skipped whole,\n66:as are blocks whose pair evidence would exceed the 128-owner record bound.\n68:skipped block count. Byte accounting advances only with the newly admitted\n69:block rather than rescanning the accumulated store. This is a bounded\n79:The final Phase 1 real-corpus dry-run against `entire-graph` (2026-08-23)\n81:exports; candidate mode deterministically coalesces same-branch re-exports to\n85:reconciliation calls. The intentionally unbatched attribution contract produced\n86:368 extraction calls versus 731 legacy extraction calls (or up to 1,462\n87:extraction-plus-reconciliation calls). This is evidence that deterministic\n89:remained necessary before a 30-60-call claim.\n91:### Phase 2 evidence (2026-08-23)\n97:packer remains the Phase 2 protocol ceiling. The proven local Ollama policy\n98:plans 111 two-member packs when cold: 84.8 percent fewer extraction calls than\n99:the 731-call legacy baseline, or 92.4 percent fewer calls than the 1,462-call\n113:fact. Phase 2 now uses a dedicated non-conflicting prompt and accepts only that\n116:completed one packed call in 10.66 seconds, reported 2,497 input and 150 output\n118:zero-call member-cache hit in 37 milliseconds. A task-local “do not change any\n119:files or code” request found during the same audit is now deterministically\n122:This passes the implementation, isolation, fixed-policy call-count, and small\n123:real-provider protocol checks. It does **not** pass Phase 2's full exit gate:\n125:still requires the human-labeled span recall/precision audit, filtered-out\n126:negative sample, repeated paired legacy/candidate provider runs, source-anchor\n129:#### Sealed advisory panel before human adjudication (2026-08-25)\n131:The next Phase 2 slice adds a reproducible pre-adjudication workflow, not an\n132:automated proof label. `facts distill-quality prepare` seals one redacted local\n140:paths, branches, session ids, checkpoints, cache keys, credentials, and human\n143:`facts distill-quality judge` submits that identical sealed packet set to\n145:verdicts and to eventual human labels, validates exact packet and payload\n152:`facts distill-quality report` produces a concise `human-review.md` start page,\n153:the complete `human-review-audit.md` evidence archive, raw per-judge score\n155:deliberately exhaustive and is **not** the human review interface.\n159:entire brain facts distill-quality adjudicate \\\n160:  --bundle <quality-run-directory> \\\n164:The default session is a deterministic 20-item calibration batch balanced\n167:starts with the exact human statement selected or filtered by candidate\n179:correct. The stored human record claims only the resulting admission label;\n180:authority, safety, and downstream fact-quality dimensions remain unclaimed.\n183:Existing saved records remain valid and are skipped on resume. `--plain`\n184:remains the line-oriented accessibility/non-TTY fallback.\n186:Each explicit human answer is validated, bound to the packet and advisory\n187:digests, written atomically to a private per-reviewer JSONL file, and\n190:archive into one reading task. No panel consensus becomes a default or bulk\n193:Every model score and rationale remains advisory only: it cannot populate\n194:proof labels, pass a Phase 2 gate, or replace the required human review. Final\n195:human decisions are the sole input to the candidate-admission metrics, and the\n196:paired legacy/candidate extraction and retrieval gates still follow that\n200:`quality-run-v1:33808625a097f0e5ab411a5cddb92c337257a7b4c62c7fad7c53852dee919868`.\n222:The human report flags 221 packets with at least one critical advisory score,\n227:not error rates, because no human proof labels exist yet. The adjudication\n230:Provider execution retained all call attempts. Copilot used 34 calls (29\n232:recovery calls) and did not expose token usage. Cursor used 28 calls (23\n234:output tokens. Claude used 158 calls (83 complete, 11 schema failures, and 64\n235:transport failures), including 40 recovery calls; the bounded recovery lane\n237:Claude reported 1,806 input plus 1,454,994 output tokens, but its CLI's cached\n238:input accounting is not a complete prompt-volume measure. Summed provider-call\n242:single-call ceiling and was excluded before the sealed Claude Haiku run.\n244:#### First human calibration and selector rebase (2026-09-10)\n249:judges had no majority. The resulting human admission labels judged the filter\n252:human-labeled filtered-out miss; it is a calibration result, not the Phase 2\n253:recall or precision estimate.\n261:decisions. The one panel disagreement remains human-owned: a direct request to\n267:`distill-quality prepare --reuse-from <sealed-run>` now makes selector\n268:calibration incremental. It copies no provider-call telemetry and reuses a\n275:versions remain readable, while future schemas and changed redaction versions\n282:remain explicitly invalid after the one bounded recovery pass and are omitted\n283:from the human presentation. The final selector rebase contains 171 admitted\n286:delta packets; 18 unchanged human records migrated. No additional bulk human\n290:members, 1,119,642 candidate bytes, and zero reconciliation calls. The\n291:provider-neutral 32-member policy plans 25 extraction calls; the proven local\n293:preprocessed bytes, 801 extraction calls, and a 1,602-call\n296:96.88 percent fewer extraction calls (98.44 percent below the legacy total-call\n297:ceiling). Ollama's conservative policy remains 89.14 percent below legacy\n298:extraction calls and 94.57 percent below the total-call ceiling.\n305:### Phase 3A evidence (2026-08-23)\n307:At the Phase 3A checkpoint, source dry runs against the retained\n313:candidate bytes, one member-cache hit, 230 misses, 29 scheduled packs/calls,\n314:and zero reconciliation calls. The cache-matched legacy control reports 154\n315:exports, 33,663,145 preprocessed bytes, 730 scheduled extraction calls, and a\n316:1,460-call extraction-plus-reconciliation ceiling.\n318:On that retained cache state, Phase 3A therefore plans 95.8 percent fewer input\n319:bytes, 96.0 percent fewer extraction calls, and 98.0 percent fewer calls than\n321:dry-run measurements, not hosted-provider latency or quality claims. Focused\n322:integration tests additionally prove one packed call for two candidates, a\n323:zero-provider-call byte-stable no-op replay, a zero-call mechanics-only anchor\n327:Phase 3A's synthetic evidence was necessary but not sufficient for the Phase 3\n329:The human-labeled Phase 2 recall and precision audit, repeated paired provider\n330:runs, filtered-negative audit, and retrieval evaluation remain required before\n331:promotion or any default change.\n333:### Phase 3B evidence (2026-08-23)\n335:The first Phase 3B slice adds a 20-case sanitized admission fixture spanning\n340:the full human-labeled Phase 2 corpus gate.\n344:remain distinct, with neither an executable proposal nor a neutral\n345:relationship. Exact-write replay is byte-stable, force output matches a clean\n348:this parity gate. A separate crash-window regressi