onomy path syntax, recall\n555:## Existing Contracts To Preserve\n565:| Privacy lifecycle | session tombstones, exclude/include/purge | Excluded or purged sessions cannot produce candidates, cache hits, facts, or published metadata. |\n566:| Quality gate | `templates/entire-brain-distill.md` | Silence remains the default and the six fact kinds remain unchanged. |\n567:| Fact identity | `factmerge.RecordID` and `factmerge.Upsert` | Existing normalized text + sorted-path ids and provenance union remain valid. |\n568:| Branch scoping | resolved session branch and branch fact stores | Candidate extraction may be shared, but materialized facts remain branch-scoped. |\n570:| Cache-on-success | current session cache | A failed pack is not marked extracted; successful empty output is cacheable. |\n575:not themselves durable-fact candidates. History deliberately favors retrieval\n576:recall and can label the same assistant line as decision, learning,\n580:## Pipeline Data Model\n586:### Typed turn\n596:    Authority     string // human | assistant_claim | context_only | rejected\n615:### Candidate card\n623:  \"authority\": \"human\",\n650:### Extraction result\n655:- `empty`: the quality gate emitted no fact for this candidate;\n657:- `failed`: never persisted as a cache hit.\n662:## Stage 1: Typed Conversation Normalization\n667:### Dialect routing\n677:redacted-thinking, tool calls, tool output, patches, command output, API error\n685:### Canonical user turns\n687:The normalizer must distinguish actual human language from messages encoded\n695:  command's human arguments and suppress the generated skill body.\n696:- Parse the human portion of `<command-args>` when it exists. Do not retain\n700:  a later claim, but text inside them is not a fresh human preference.\n704:  let the quality gate reject it; do not assign human authority by default.\n708:### Canonical assistant turns\n711:itself. Preserve the request/response relationship and collect the following\n721:### Exact anchors\n732:## Stage 2: Deterministic Candidate Generation\n734:Candidate generation is a high-recall admission filter. A match means \"worth\n735:asking the quality gate,\" not \"write a fact.\"\n737:### Trigger classes\n744:| Standing rule | `from now on`, `going forward`, `always`, `never`, `whenever`, `every time`, `make sure` | high for direct human text |\n745:| Preference | `I prefer`, `we prefer`, `use X over Y`, `I want`, durable corrective feedback | high for direct human text |\n750:| Explicit revision | `not X; use Y`, `ignore the previous rule`, `we no longer`, `replace X with Y` | high for direct human text; carries a subject key |\n757:### Negative admission signals\n778:The final item preserves the existing \"not already known\" quality contract. In\n783:### Candidate scoring\n790:| Direct human standing-rule or preference phrase | +6 |\n791:| Direct human explicit revision | +6 |\n808:### Role-aware windows\n810:Build the smallest window that lets the quality gate judge resolution and\n827:AUTHORITY human\n840:## Candidate Authority And Corroboration\n842:Authority and truth are separate. A human can authoritatively express a\n843:preference, but a human statement about current code can still be stale. An\n847:### Human assertions\n849:Direct human standing rules, preferences, and explicit revisions receive the\n850:highest authority prior. They still pass the durable-fact quality gate for\n853:Imperatives in a task request do not automatically become conventions. \"Run\n858:### Assistant claims\n863:1. The next human turn explicitly accepts, corrects, or restates it.\n869:5. A later human turn cites the claim as established context.\n875:default. A review claim can become eligible only after a later accepted fix,\n876:human confirmation, or matching committed change. The original review remains\n879:### Deterministic evidence envelope\n895:## Stage 3: Candidate Packing And Fact Extraction\n897:The existing distill prompt remains the source of the