tion. Candidate mode exposes an\n1262:  additive pack-byte limit only if measurement shows the default cannot be\n1268:- Changing `--confidence` replays application without agent calls.\n1271:### Rollback\n1273:Before candidate mode becomes default, a user can select `--pipeline legacy`\n1274:without deleting candidate cache state. The schema-v3 manifest is decoded\n1280:## Observability And Cost Accounting\n1307:- cache hit/miss counts and bytes avoided for every stage;\n1308:- extraction calls, token usage, wait time, and facts emitted;\n1313:Warnings remain bounded by the existing warning cap. A candidate id, rule id,\n1316:Provider token accounting remains provider-reported and keeps completeness\n1319:prompt/taxonomy digests, cache state, and claim scope.\n1321:## Evaluation Design And Admission Gates\n1327:### Gold corpus\n1333:- direct human preferences and standing rules;\n1350:- should emit or should remain silent;\n1356:- expected relationship to existing facts.\n1361:### Candidate-generation gates\n1363:- At least 98 percent span recall for explicit human standing rules,\n1365:- At least 95 percent span recall across all gold durable facts.\n1367:- No direct-human turn may be reclassified as generated solely because it uses\n1373:  set and blocks default rollout until addressed.\n1377:quality gate offline during evaluation. Review any fact it emits that candidate\n1381:### Fact-quality gates\n1383:Run paired legacy and candidate extraction with the same prompt, taxonomy,\n1389:- durable-fact precision and recall;\n1391:- human-authority and corroboration correctness;\n1401:- Candidate mode is non-inferior to legacy fact recall within a predeclared\n1411:### Retrieval gates\n1414:facts per 1,000 tokens, precision, recall, and answer support. Candidate mode\n1415:must not claim a retrieval win unless proof-labeled paired evaluation supports\n1421:- no more than a two-percentage-point absolute recall loss against legacy\n1423:- regression tasks for every current live-corpus quality failure;\n1425:  better retrieval merely because output is shorter.\n1427:### Operational gates\n1431:- at least 80 percent fewer extraction calls than 64 KiB legacy mode;\n1432:- at least 90 percent fewer total agent calls than the extraction-plus-reconcile\n1435:- no reconcile-agent calls in candidate mode;\n1436:- a no-op rerun makes zero provider calls;\n1437:- appending a no-candidate turn makes zero provider calls;\n1438:- appending one isolated candidate makes at most one provider pack call;\n1439:- transcript relocation and branch replay make zero extraction calls;\n1440:- a confidence-threshold change makes zero provider calls;\n1446:corrupt-cache scenarios as integration tests.\n1448:## Rollout Plan\n1450:### Phase 0: Measurement-only candidate planner\n1453:- Emit the full funnel and projected packs without making an agent call or\n1454:  writing v2 cache/facts.\n1459:Exit gate: canonical read safety and dry-run determinism pass; candidate recall\n1462:### Phase 1: Typed turns and content-addressed discovery cache\n1465:  changing conversation retrieval behavior.\n1473:- new `internal/cli/distill_cache_v2.go`;\n1478:Exit gate: no plaintext card cache, no privacy regression, exact duplicate and\n1481:### Phase 2: Candidate-pack extraction, shadow only\n1488:- Compare outputs with legacy extraction and human labels.\n1490:Exit gate: candidate and fact-quality gates pass on the full labeled corpus;\n1491:token/call accounting is complete.\n1493:### Phase 3: Conservative reconciliation and opt-in writes\n1496:- Phase 3A ships exact-only reconciliation first and keeps all different ids\n1498:- Keep the Phase 3B evidence-bearing neutral relationship store local,\n1500:- Validate neutral relationship precision and lifecycle parity on the labeled\n1505:Exit gate (met 2026-08-23): all live-corpus bad-reconcile fixtures pass,\n1508:tracked separately by the still-open Phase 2 quality gate.\n1510:### Phase 4: Session-end incremental candidate distill\n1517:Exit gate: no-candidate session end is zero-call and one-candidate session end is\n1518:at most one pack call under normal cache state.\n1520:### Phase 5: Default rollout\n1522:- Retain candidate dry-run and paired release evidence on a small, medium, and\n1524:- Make candidate mode the default only after all quality, retrieval,\n1527:- Do not describe distillation as fast, cheaper, or recall-preserving beyond the\n1530:## Implementation Order And Test Map\n1538:5. Add v2 content-addressed cache and append/purge tests.\n1540:7. Add deterministic packing, member cache, split retry, and concurrency tests.\n1558:- cache-on-success, empty-result caching, split retry, crash/resume, and corrupt\n1559:  cache;\n1565:- retained `entire-graph` cost and quality regression fixtures.\n1567:## Decisions Locked By This Plan\n1570:- Fact extraction remains agent-gated and silent by default.\n1573:- Candidate identity and extraction identity are separate cache layers.\n1578:- Legacy mode remains available until candidate mode has retained quality and\n1581:## Open Questions To Resolve With Evidence\n1590:  should v1 remain exact-only indefinitely?\n1592:  and where must normalized-content fallback identity remain explicit?\n1593:- How much adjacent context is needed for closed negatives and human acceptance\n1599:These questions do not block Phase 0. They block progressively broader\n1600:automation and the default switch, and each has an explicit measurement point\n"},"started_at_ms":1789067577632,"completed_at_ms":1789067577632}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:12:57.688Z","ordinal":38211,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a08cbc-c958-7411-b110-bd1fb6ce3b5c","call_id":"call_IIsjFAtId40aCHzeXvaieCIc","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"1:# Candidate-First Distillation Plan\n3:Status: Phase 3 conservative-write exit gate complete. Phase 2 has a sealed\n4:advisory multi-model pre-adjudication package, a resumable human review\n6:human-labeled audit, paired fact-quality runs, and retrieval gates remain\n7:pending and block default promotion (2026-09-10).\n11:direct-user candidate cards, one card per extraction call, conservative exact\n12:upserts with no reconciliation-agent call, separate rollback-safe session-cache\n14:Legacy remains the default.\n16:The Phase 2 branch adds candidate-id-framed multi-card output, deterministic\n18:a bounded success-only member cache, one-level failure bisection, provider usage\n20:taxonomy, the legacy cache, and the manifest unchanged. Exclude/purge resets the\n21:derived member cache; privacy verification, atomic-temp cleanup, and publish\n28:The Phase 3A branch routes opt-in non-shadow candidate runs through that same\n29:framed, packed, member-cached extraction path. It materializes only exact fact\n37:artifact. Different fact ids remain separate with no automatic merge or\n40:Phase 3B adds that evidence-bearing shape without changing reconciliation. A\n47:`facts/distill-v2/relationships.ndjson` and is exposed only through the\n48:read-only `facts relationships list` command. It has no action, confidence,\n50:publication path. Executable merge/supersede proposals remain unchanged and\n61:fail merely because a subject is broad. It indexes exact subject blocks, sorts\n62:them deterministically, and admits a block only when its complete pair set fits\n63:the remaining 4,096-entry and 4 MiB store budgets. A 91-member block (4,095\n64:pairs) is admissible; a 92-member block (4,186 pairs) is skipped before pair\n65:enumeration. Byte- or capacity-limited blocks are likewise skipped whole,\n66:as are blocks whose pair evidence would exceed the 128-owner record bound.\n68:skipped block count. Byte accounting advances only with the newly admitted\n69:block rather than rescanning the accumulated store. This is a bounded\n79:The final Phase 1 real-corpus dry-run against `entire-graph` (2026-08-23)\n81:exports; candidate mode deterministically coalesces same-branch re-exports to\n85:reconciliation calls. The intentionally unbatched attribution contract produced\n86:368 extraction calls versus 731 legacy extraction calls (or up to 1,462\n87:extraction-plus-reconciliation calls). This is evidence that deterministic\n89:remained necessary before a 30-60-call claim.\n91:### Phase 2 evidence (2026-08-23)\n97:packer remains the Phase 2 protocol ceiling. The proven local Ollama policy\n98:plans 111 two-member packs when cold: 84.8 percent fewer extraction calls than\n99:the 731-call legacy baseline, or 92.4 percent fewer calls than the 1,462-call\n113:fact. Phase 2 now uses a dedicated non-conflicting prompt and accepts only that\n116:completed one packed call in 10.66 seconds, reported 2,497 input and 150 output\n118:zero-call member-cache hit in 37 milliseconds. A task-local “do not change any\n119:files or code” request found during the same audit is now deterministically\n122:This passes the implementation, isolation, fixed-policy call-count, and small\n123:real-provider protocol checks. It does **not** pass Phase 2's full exit gate:\n125:still requires the human-labeled span recall/precision audit, filtered-out\n126:negative sample, repeated paired legacy/candidate provider runs, source-anchor\n129:#### Sealed advisory panel before human adjudication (2026-08-25)\n131:The next Phase 2 slice adds a reproducible pre-adjudication workflow, not an\n132:automated proof label. `facts distill-quality prepare` seals one redacted local\n140:paths, branches, session ids, checkpoints, cache keys, credentials, and human\n143:`facts distill-quality judge` submits that identical sealed packet set to\n145:verdicts and to eventual human labels, validates exact packet and payload\n152:`facts distill-quality report` produces a concise `human-review.md` start page,\n153:the complete `human-review-audit.md` evidence archive, raw per-judge score\n155:deliberately exhaustive and is **not** the human review interface.\n159:entire brain facts distill-quality adjudicate \\\n160:  --bundle <quality-run-directory> \\\n164:The default session is a deterministic 20-item calibration batch balanced\n167:starts with the exact human statement selected or filtered by candidate\n179:correct. The stored human record claims only the resulting admission label;\n180:authority, safety, and downstream fact-quality dimensions remain unclaimed.\n183:Existing saved records remain valid and are skipped on resume. `--plain`\n184:remains the line-oriented accessibility/non-TTY fallback.\n186:Each explicit human answer is validated, bound to the packet and advisory\n187:digests, written atomically to a private per-reviewer JSONL file, and\n190:archive into one reading task. No panel consensus becomes a default or bulk\n193:Every model score and rationale remains advisory only: it cannot populate\n194:proof labels, pass a Phase 2 gate, or replace the required human review. Final\n195:human decisions are the sole input to the candidate-admission metrics, and the\n196:paired legacy/candidate extraction and retrieval gates still follow that\n200:`quality-run-v1:33808625a097f0e5ab411a5cddb92c337257a7b4c62c7fad7c53852dee919868`.\n222:The human report flags 221 packets with at least one critical advisory score,\n227:not error rates, because no human proof labels exist yet. The adjudication\n230:Provider execution retained all call attempts. Copilot used 34 calls (29\n232:recovery calls) and did not expose token usage. Cursor