variance is an observed Phase 2 provider-quality failure, not evidence of\n377:Phase 3 parity, and it remains a release/default blocker. Phase 3 application\n381:stores had identical 356 facts and all 355 application receipts; relationship\n383:zero-call and byte-stable.\n388:superseded fact remained the only superseded fact, and executable proposals\n389:remained empty. Sanitized regressions retain the historical `--no-network`\n392:Every live neutral relationship was joined back to its fact pair for manual\n396:remaining seven observations across the two provider runs were narrow\n400:from current v2-owned facts with zero provider calls instead of blocking fact\n401:application; privacy verification remains fail-closed.\n403:These results satisfy the Phase 3 exit gate: the retained bad-reconciliation\n406:Phase 2's fact-quality, repeated-provider, filtered-negative, or retrieval\n407:gates, so candidate mode remains opt-in and legacy remains the default.\n412:only those windows to the selected fact agent. Fact quality, taxonomy,\n413:branch-scoping, provenance, review, and recall remain durable-facts contracts;\n414:the unit of model work and cache invalidation changes from a whole session to a\n424:  -> durable-fact quality/classification    fact agent, candidate text only\n429:The raw transcript remains the retained source of truth. Candidate cards and\n433:## Why This Work Is Needed\n435:The current pipeline already removes tool calls, tool output, reasoning, and\n437:but every remaining user and assistant line is still sent to a fact agent in\n440:candidate-bearing chunk may then cause a second agent call to reconcile its\n444:cannot distinguish a human standing rule from an assistant's tentative review\n449:### Measured `entire-graph` baseline\n460:| Extraction calls at the default 48 KiB chunk size | 731 |\n461:| Total call upper bound at 48 KiB, including reconcile | 1,462 |\n462:| Uncached chunks at the measured 64 KiB Ollama configuration | 580 |\n463:| Scheduled extraction calls at 64 KiB | 579 |\n464:| Total scheduled-call upper bound at 64 KiB | 1,158 |\n465:| Sessions cached under that exact configuration | 1 of 154 |\n468:extraction call and one reconcile call, reported 7,179 provider tokens, and took\n477:  cache can reuse their unchanged prefixes even when a whole-file digest cannot.\n493:### Quality findings from the live fact store\n504:- near-duplicate `--no-network` facts remained active under different wording;\n509:key and that assistant text cannot inherit human authority merely because it is\n512:## Goals\n516:- Preserve at least 98 percent candidate recall for explicit user standing\n518:  recall across all human-labeled durable facts before the agent runs.\n519:- Preserve the existing silent quality gate: most candidate cards should still\n521:- Keep facts source-backed, branch-aware, content-addressed, locally\n528:  paraphrases should merge deterministically; uncertain relationships should\n529:  remain visible for review.\n531:  observability, and cache preparation. Fact extraction remains agent-gated.\n532:- Reduce input tokens by 85-95 percent and total agent calls by at least 90\n534:  recall regression.\n536:## Non-Goals\n539:  admit candidates; the existing durable-fact quality and classification gate\n542:  An unconditional session-summary call has the same wrong default at a smaller\n544:- Do not treat assistant review findings, plans, or status reports as human\n549:- Do not store a second plaintext transcript archive in candidate caches.\n551:- Do not change authored-fact semantics, fact ids, taxonomy path syntax, recall\n555:## Existing Contracts To Preserve\n565:| Privacy lifecycle | session tombstones, exclude/include/purge | Excluded or purged sessions cannot produce candidates, cache hits, facts, or published metadata. |\n566:| Quality gate | `templates/entire-brain-distill.md` | Silence remains the default and the six fact kinds remain unchanged. |\n567:| Fact identity | `factmerge.RecordID` and `factmerge.Upsert` | Existing normalized text + sorted-path ids and provenance union remain valid. |\n568:| Branch scoping | resolved session branch and branch fact stores | Candidate extraction may be shared, but materialized facts remain branch-scoped. |\n570:| Cache-on-success | current session cache | A failed pack is not marked extracted; successful empty output is cacheable. |\n575:not themselves durable-fact candidates. History deliberately favors retrieval\n576:recall and can label the same assistant line as decision, learning,\n580:## Pipeline Data Model\n586:### Typed turn\n596:    Authority     string // human | assistant_claim | context_only | rejected\n615:### Candidate card\n623:  \"authority\": \"human\",\n650:### Extraction result\n655:- `empty`: the quality gate emitted no fact for this candidate;\n657:- `failed`: never persisted as a cache hit.\n662:## Stage 1: Typed Conversation Normalization\n667:### Dialect routing\n677:redacted-thinking, tool calls, tool output, patches, command output, API error\n685:### Canonical user turns\n687:The normalizer must distinguish actual human language from messages encoded\n695:  command's human arguments and suppress the generated skill body.\n696:- Parse the human portion of `<command-args>` when it exists. Do not retain\n700:  a later claim, but text inside them is not a fresh human preference.\n704:  let the quality gate reject it; do not assign human authority by default.\n708:### Canonical assistant turns\n711:itself. Preserve the request/response relationship and collect the following\n721:### Exact anchors\n732:## Stage 2: Deterministic Candidate Generation\n734:Candidate generation is a high-recall admission filter. A match means \"worth\n735:asking the quality gate,\" not \"write a fact.\"\n737:### Trigger classes\n744:| Standing rule | `from now on`, `going forward`, `always`, `never`, `whenever`, `every time`, `make sure` | high for direct human text |\n745:| Preference | `I prefer`, `we prefer`, `use X over Y`, `I want`, durable corrective feedback | high for direct human text |\n750:| Explicit revision | `not X; use Y`, `ignore the previous rule`, `we no longer`, `replace X with Y` | high for direct human text; carries a subject key |\n757:### Negative admission signals\n778:The final item preserves the existing \"not already known\" quality contract. In\n783:### Candidate scoring\n790:| Direct human standing-rule or preference phrase | +6 |\n791:| Direct human explicit revision | +6 |\n808:### Role-aware windows\n810:Build the smallest window that lets the quality gate judge resolution and\n827:AUTHORITY human\n840:## Candidate Authority And Corroboration\n842:Authority and truth are separate. A human can authoritatively express a\n843:preference, but a human statement about current code can still be stale. An\n847:### Human assertions\n849:Direct human standing rules, preferences, and explicit revisions receive the\n850:highest authority prior. They still pass the durable-fact quality gate for\n853:Imperatives in a task request do not automatically become conventions. \"Run\n858:### Assistant claims\n863:1. The next human turn explicitly accepts, corrects, or restates it.\n869:5. A later human turn cites the claim as established context.\n875:default. A review claim can become eligible only after a later accepted fix,\n876:human confirmation, or matching committed change. The original review remains\n879:### Deterministic evidence envelope\n895:## Stage 3: Candidate Packing And Fact Extraction\n897:The existing distill prompt remains the source of the durable-fact gate and\n911:### Pack construction\n924:### Failure isolation\n935:### Expected call shape\n939:extraction calls instead of 579 at 64 KiB, about 90 percent fewer. Cross-session\n940:packing should reduce that further to approximately 30-60 extraction calls.\n942:The candidate pipeline makes no routine reconcile calls. Against the current\n943:upper bound of 1,158 extraction-plus-reconcile calls, 30-60 total calls is a\n947:## Stage 4: Stage-Separated Content-Addressed Cache\n949:The current cache answers one coarse question: \"was this whole session\n951:effort, branch, checkpoint, and preprocessed content?\" Candidate-first cache\n954:### Cache layers\n970:### Append behavior\n984:Whole-session reprocessing remains the safe fallback for an unsupported or\n987:### Persistence and interruption\n993:  distill-cache.json                 # legacy v1, unchanged\n1006:The pipeline may prepare and call agents outside the global write lock, as it\n1010:## Stage 5: Conservative Deterministic Reconciliation\n1012:The candidate pipeline removes the default reconcile-agent call. It uses a\n1015:### Step 1: Exact identity\n1020:### Step 2: Safe paraphrase block\n1022:Only compare different ids when they share a semantic subject block:\n1028:A taxonomy path alone is not a block key. Broad paths such as\n1031:Within the block, deterministic normalization may merge only obvious\n1040:The earlier fact text remains canonical and provenance is unioned. Every\n1043:### Step 3: Supersession\n1050:- the newer source has direct human authority or an accepted assistant claim;\n1060:### Step 4: New fact\n1062:If no exact or safe paraphrase relationship exists, add the candidate as new.\n1065:### Review behavior\n1067:Proposal dedup remains `(action, candidate, target)`. Repeated evidence can add\n1069:the deterministic subject block, similarity features, authority, and source\n1070:chronology so a human can resolve it without rereading whole sessions.\n1072:## Branches, Checkpoints, And Provenance\n1081:- Branch- and session-limited distill runs carry untouched cache and fact state\n1088:Chronological application order remains source session creation time, then turn\n1092:## Storage And Privacy\n1097:### No second transcript store\n1102:- Extraction cache fact text is equivalent in sensitivity to the durable fact\n1107:### Egress\n1113:  and Claude tool disabling, timeouts, and output limits remain unchanged.\n1114:- Dry run and candidate planning make no agent or network call.\n1116:### Exclude, tombstone, and purge\n1118:Before planning or cache lookup, filter tombstoned sessions. A cache hit is\n1133:Bundles and publish output exclude all `distill-v2` caches by default. Durable\n1137:### Canonical-read safety\n1139:Keep complete-or-refused preflight before provider calls or any incremental\n1143:## CLI And Manifest Contract\n1153:During experimentation, `legacy` remains the default. After all gates pass,\n1154:`candidate` becomes the default and `legacy` remains a compatibility/debugging\n1171:  \"cache\": {\n1178:    \"human\": 12,\n1187:  \"estimated_extraction_calls\": 57,\n1188:  \"estimated_reconcile_calls\": 0\n1192:Field values above illustrate the target contract. Legacy fields remain present\n1206:- stage cache hits and misses;\n1213:whether candidate cache state is current, stale, partially reusable, or\n1215:admitted, packs completed, facts found, and cache hits without printing\n1218:## Migration And Compatibility\n1220:### Fact store\n1243:### Cache\n1245:Keep `facts/distill-cache.json` for the legacy pipeline. Do not rewrite v1\n1246:entries into v2 keys: the two caches prove different work. The first v2 run\n1247:builds typed and candidate metadata locally, then reuses existing facts through\n1250:A corrupt or unsupported v2 cache falls back to deterministic reconstruction.\n1251:It never causes legacy cache deletion or fact-store truncation. New v2 schema\n1255:### Flags\n1261:- `--max-chunk-bytes` remains a legacy option. Candidate mode exposes an\n1262:  additive pack-byte limit only if measurement shows the default cannot be\n1268:- Changing `--confidence` replays application without agent calls.\n1271:### Rollback\n1273:Before candidate mode becomes default, a user can select `--pipeline legacy`\n1274:without deleting candidate cache state. The schema-v3 manifest is decoded\n1280:## Observability And Cost Accounting\n1307:- cache hit/miss counts and bytes avoided for every stage;\n1308:- extraction calls, token usage, wait time, and facts emitted;\n1313:Warnings remain bounded by the existing warning cap. A candidate id, rule id,\n1316:Provider token accounting remains provider-reported and keeps completeness\n1319:prompt/taxonomy digests, cache state, and claim scope.\n1321:## Evaluation Design And Admission Gates\n1327:### Gold corpus\n1333:- direct human preferences and standing rules;\n1350:- should emit or should remain silent;\n1356:- expected relationship to existing facts.\n1361:### Candidate-generation gates\n1363:- At least 98 percent span recall for explicit human standing rules,\n1365:- At least 95 percent span recall across all gold durable facts.\n1367:- No direct-human turn may be reclassified as generated solely because it uses\n1373:  set and blocks default rollout until addressed.\n1377:quality gate offline during evaluation. Review any fact it emits that candidate\n1381:### Fact-quality gates\n1383:Run paired legacy and candidate extraction with the same prompt, taxonomy,\n1389:- durable-fact precision and recall;\n1391:- human-authority and corroboration correctness;\n1401:- Candidate mode is non-inferior to legacy fact recall within a predeclared\n1411:### Retrieval gates\n1414:facts per 1,000 tokens, precision, recall, and answer support. Candidate mode\n1415:must not claim a retrieval win unless proof-labeled paired evaluation supports\n1421:- no more than a two-percentage-point absolute recall loss against legacy\n1423:- regression tasks for every current live-corpus quality failure;\n1425:  better retrieval merely because output is shorter.\n1427:### Operational gates\n1431:- at least 80 percent fewer extraction calls than 64 KiB legacy mode;\n1432:- at least 90 percent fewer total agent calls than the extraction-plus-reconcile\n1435:- no reconcile-agent calls in candidate mode;\n1436:- a no-op rerun makes zero provider calls;\n1437:- appending a no-candidate turn makes zero provider calls;\n1438:- appending one isolated candidate makes at most one provider pack call;\n1439:- transcript relocation and branch replay make zero extraction calls;\n1440:- a confidence-threshold change makes zero provider calls;\n1446:corrupt-cache scenarios as integration tests.\n1448:## Rollout Plan\n1450:### Phase 0: Measurement-only candidate planner\n1453:- Emit the full funnel and projected packs without making an agent call or\n1454:  writing v2 cache/facts.\n1459:Exit gate: canonical read safety and dry-run determinism pass; candidate recall\n1462:### Phase 1: Typed turns and content-addressed discovery cache\n1465:  changing conversation retrieval behavior.\n1473:- new `internal/cli/distill_cache_v2.go`;\n1478:Exit gate: no plaintext card cache, no privacy regression, exact duplicate and\n1481:### Phase 2: Candidate-pack extraction, shadow only\n1488:- Compare outputs with legacy extraction and human labels.\n1490:Exit gate: candidate and fact-quality gates pass on the full labeled corpus;\n1491:token/call accounting is complete.\n1493:### Phase 3: Conservative reconciliation and opt-in writes\n1496:- Phase 3A ships exact-only reconciliation first and keeps all different ids\n1498:- Keep the Phase 3B evidence-bearing neutral relationship store local,\n1500:- Validate neutral relationship precision and lifecycle parity on the labeled\n1505:Exit gate (met 2026-08-23): all live-corpus bad-reconcile fixtures pass,\n1508:tracked separately by the still-open Phase 2 quality gate.\n1510:### Phase 4: Session-end incremental candidate distill\n1517:Exit gate: no-candidate session end is zero-call and one-candidate session end is\n1518:at most one pack call under normal cache state.\n1520:### Phase 5: Default rollout\n1522:- Retain candidate dry-run and paired release evidence on a small, medium, and\n1524:- Make candidate mode the default only after all quality, retrieval,\n1527:- Do not describe distillation as fast, cheaper, or recall-preserving beyond the\n1530:## Implementation Order And Test Map\n1538:5. Add v2 content-addressed cache and append/purge tests.\n1540:7. Add deterministic packing, member cache, split retry, and concurrency tests.\n1558:- cache-on-success, empty-result caching, split retry, crash/resume, and corrupt\n1559:  cache;\n1565:- retained `entire-graph` cost and quality regression fixtures.\n1567:## Decisions Locked By This Plan\n1570:- Fact extraction remains agent-gated and silent by default.\n1573:- Candidate identity and extraction identity are separate cache layers.\n1578:- Legacy mode remains available until candidate mode has retained quality and\n1581:## Open Questions To Resolve With Evidence\n1590:  should v1 remain exact-only indefinitely?\n1592:  and where must normalized-content fallback identity remain explicit?\n1593:- How much adjacent context is needed for closed negatives and human acceptance\n1599:These questions do not block Phase 0. They block progressively broader\n1600:automation and the default switch, and each has an explicit measurement point\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08cbc-3e2e-71d0-bf78-c2587ebbc22c"}}}
