{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:16:25.447Z","ordinal":38256,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0200a-63d8-7b21-adef-c3850aecebf7","turn_id":"01a08cbc-3e2e-71d0-bf78-c2587ebbc22c","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0873a68aa02aff8f016aa301fd72788198ab03451e9e159caf","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The implementation through Phase 3 is largely complete. What remains is:\n\n| Phase | Status | Remaining |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0–1 | Engineering complete | Their original gold-corpus requirement rolled into the open Phase 2 gate. |\n| 2 | Machinery complete, exit gate open | Representative human labels, paired extraction runs, retrieval evaluation, and complete provider telemetry. |\n| 3 | Complete | Exact-only writes, receipts, lifecycle parity, and neutral relationships passed. |\n| 4 | Not implemented | Candidate-first incremental session-end distillation. |\n| 5 | Not started | Multi-corpus release evidence and default rollout. |\n\nThe critical remaining work is:\n\n1. Finish Phase 2 quality evidence\n\n   - Build a representative exact-span gold corpus, including filtered-out examples.\n   - Audit at least 500 filtered exchanges for critical misses.\n   - Run legacy and candidate extraction with identical settings, repeated three times.\n   - Human-score facts, anchors, authority, taxonomy, duplicates, and exclusions.\n   - Establish ≥98% explicit-rule recall, ≥95% overall durable-fact recall, and non-inferiority to legacy within two percentage points.\n   - Capture complete token, latency, and failure telemetry.\n\n   The completed 20-item review was selector calibration only. It found useful errors, but cannot measure recall or extraction quality. The observed 419-versus-356 fact variance between provider runs remains the main known quality blocker. See [evaluation gates](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1321).\n\n2. Run the retrieval gate\n\n   Compare candidate and legacy stores for useful facts per 1,000 tokens, recall, precision, and answer support. Candidate recall may lose no more than two absolute percentage points. See [retrieval gates](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1411).\n\n3. Close one remaining candidate-generation limitation\n\n   Oversized authoritative turns currently fail safely rather than truncate. They need cue-span or paragraph splitting before candidate mode is corpus-general. See [oversized-turn limitation](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:72).\n\n4. Implement Phase 4\n\n   Route `session-end` through candidate discovery, process only the append boundary, reuse results across branch exports, and prove:\n\n   - no candidate → zero provider calls;\n   - one candidate → at most one pack call.\n\n   The hook still defaults to the legacy pipeline. See [Phase 4](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1510).\n\n5. Complete Phase 5\n\n   Retain paired evidence across small, medium, and large repositories, pass all quality/retrieval/operational/privacy gates, switch the default, and retain legacy rollback for at least one release. See [Phase 5](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1520).\n\nSafe paraphrase merging and automatic different-ID supersession are optional. Exact-only can ship if paraphrase precision does not clear 99%.\n\nSo the immediate critical path is: oversized-span handling → representative Phase 2 evaluation → retrieval gate → Phase 4 → default-rollout evidence."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1789067773432,"completed_at_ms":1789067785447}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:16:25.452Z","ordinal":38257,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0873a68aa02aff8f016aa301fd72788198ab03451e9e159caf","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The implementation through Phase 3 is largely complete. What remains is:\n\n| Phase | Status | Remaining |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0–1 | Engineering complete | Their original gold-corpus requirement rolled into the open Phase 2 gate. |\n| 2 | Machinery complete, exit gate open | Representative human labels, paired extraction runs, retrieval evaluation, and complete provider telemetry. |\n| 3 | Complete | Exact-only writes, receipts, lifecycle parity, and neutral relationships passed. |\n| 4 | Not implemented | Candidate-first incremental session-end distillation. |\n| 5 | Not started | Multi-corpus release evidence and default rollout. |\n\nThe critical remaining work is:\n\n1. Finish Phase 2 quality evidence\n\n   - Build a representative exact-span gold corpus, including filtered-out examples.\n   - Audit at least 500 filtered exchanges for critical misses.\n   - Run legacy and candidate extraction with identical settings, repeated three times.\n   - Human-score facts, anchors, authority, taxonomy, duplicates, and exclusions.\n   - Establish ≥98% explicit-rule recall, ≥95% overall durable-fact recall, and non-inferiority to legacy within two percentage points.\n   - Capture complete token, latency, and failure telemetry.\n\n   The completed 20-item review was selector calibration only. It found useful errors, but cannot measure recall or extraction quality. The observed 419-versus-356 fact variance between provider runs remains the main known quality blocker. See [evaluation gates](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1321).\n\n2. Run the retrieval gate\n\n   Compare candidate and legacy stores for useful facts per 1,000 tokens, recall, precision, and answer support. Candidate recall may lose no more than two absolute percentage points. See [retrieval gates](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1411).\n\n3. Close one remaining candidate-generation limitation\n\n   Oversized authoritative turns currently fail safely rather than truncate. They need cue-span or paragraph splitting before candidate mode is corpus-general. See [oversized-turn limitation](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:72).\n\n4. Implement Phase 4\n\n   Route `session-end` through candidate discovery, process only the append boundary, reuse results across branch exports, and prove:\n\n   - no candidate → zero provider calls;\n   - one candidate → at most one pack call.\n\n   The hook still defaults to the legacy pipeline. See [Phase 4](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1510).\n\n5. Complete Phase 5\n\n   Retain paired evidence across small, medium, and large repositories, pass all quality/retrieval/operational/privacy gates, switch the default, and retain legacy rollback for at least one release. See [Phase 5](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1520).\n\nSafe paraphrase merging and automatic different-ID supersession are optional. Exact-only can ship if paraphrase precision does not clear 99%.\n\nSo the immediate critical path is: oversized-span handling → representative Phase 2 evaluation → retrieval gate → Phase 4 → default-rollout evidence."}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08cbc-3e2e-71d0-bf78-c2587ebbc22c"}}}
