{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T20:35:50.913Z","ordinal":38302,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a08d08-ac01-7132-b097-2457002d8dd6","call_id":"call_AU9q2iPgHHbgaKXnnJbfAhPc","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/phase2_delta_impl\",\"agent_status\":\"interrupted\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/remaining_plan_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"All references are to [candidate_distillation_plan.md](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md).\\n\\nThe plan’s headline is unambiguous: Phase 3’s conservative-write exit gate is complete, while the representative human audit, paired fact-quality runs, and retrieval gates remain pending and block default promotion (L3–7). Legacy is still the default (L14, L403–407).\\n\\nWhat remains:\\n\\n### Implementation work\\n\\n- **Phase 4 is not marked complete and has no evidence section.** Remaining work is routing the session-end hook through candidate discovery, append-boundary-only parsing, cross-branch extraction reuse, and preserving watch/no-egress behavior (L1510–1515). Its exit gate—zero calls for no-candidate endings and at most one pack call for one candidate—remains unproven (L1517–1518).\\n- **Oversized authoritative turns still need cue-span/paragraph splitting** before the pipeline is corpus-general (L72–77). This is the clearest concrete candidate-generation implementation gap.\\n- **Phase 5 mechanics remain:** switch the default only after all gates, retain legacy for at least one release, and document rollback (L1520–1528).\\n- **Durable run/status observability is deferred.** A separately versioned distill-run metrics leaf and corresponding `facts status` state/progress reporting are explicitly future work (L1200–1216, L1273–1278). The implementation-order list still includes manifest/status fields and the watch/session-end path (L1543–1544).\\n- **Safe paraphrase merging is deferred and optional.** It may be added only after ≥99% pairwise precision; otherwise exact-only is explicitly acceptable (L1405–1406, L1502, L1542). It is not inherently a default blocker if v1 stays exact-only.\\n- **Automatic different-ID supersession is also deferred/non-MVP**, with exact-only behavior currently intentional (L1045–1058, L1577). Likewise, stage-specific repair is explicitly not required for the MVP (L1266–1267).\\n- **Neutral relationships cannot gain a downstream consumer yet.** Full labeled/live precision and lifecycle validation is required before that (L1500–1501); the synthetic fixture explicitly did not satisfy pairwise precision (L358–359). This does not block keeping the store local/list-only.\\n\\n### Evaluation and retained-evidence work\\n\\n- **Phase 0 is not formally closed.** The span-labeled gold set and negative-audit set remain to be built (L1457), and the first-gold-slice candidate-recall exit gate remains unmet (L1459–1460). The completed 20-item calibration contained no labeled filtered-out miss and is explicitly “not the Phase 2 recall or precision estimate” (L244–253).\\n- **The full gold corpus must cover all listed session/fact/authority/dialect cases, audit current `entire-graph` facts, record exact spans and expected outputs, and use two reviewers on ambiguous labels** (L1327–1359).\\n- **All full-corpus candidate-generation gates remain to be established:** 98% explicit-rule recall, 95% overall durable-fact recall, 100% injection rejection, correct handling of direct-human imperatives, byte-identical determinism, and a stratified audit of at least 500 filtered exchanges with zero critical misses (L1361–1373). The evaluation-only sampled legacy shadow lane for implicit decisions also remains (L1375–1379).\\n- **Phase 2’s implementation is present, but its exit gate is still open.** The document says framing/packing/isolation and a small real-provider smoke pass, but one fact is not a labeled corpus (L122–127). Advisory model judgments cannot pass the gate or replace human review (L193–197), and the sealed template began with null labels (L222–228).\\n- **Paired fact-quality evaluation remains:** legacy and candidate must run with identical settings, with at least three repeats for nondeterministic providers (L1381–1385), measuring every dimension at L1387–1397 and passing all gates at L1399–1409. The observed 419-vs-356 two-run variance is explicitly a release/default blocker (L375–377).\\n- **Token/accounting completeness remains incomplete.** Copilot exposed no token usage, and Claude’s cached-input reporting was incomplete (L230–242), while Phase 2 requires complete token/call accounting (L1490–1491).\\n- **Retrieval evaluation is entirely pending:** paired useful-facts-per-1k, precision, recall, answer support, ≤2-point recall loss, regression tasks, and retained source-session baselines (L1411–1425).\\n- **Operational gate coverage is only partial.** Proven items include call reductions, zero reconcile calls, zero-call replay, and relocation behavior (L318–325, L363–373). Still not explicitly proven are ≥85% fewer actual provider input tokens, append-no-candidate/one-candidate behavior, confidence-only replay, model/prompt/taxonomy scoped invalidation, and interruption flush-window recovery (L1427–1442). The full integration scenario matrix must also be retained (L1444–1446).\\n- **Phase 5 needs retained paired evidence on small, medium, and large corpora**, plus final quality, retrieval, operational, privacy, and migration gate signoff (L1522–1526). Privacy/lifecycle implementation evidence exists (L20–22, L35–37, L355–357), but the document does not record a consolidated Phase 5 privacy/migration signoff.\\n\\nStatus text that claims completion:\\n\\n- Phase 1’s real-corpus dry run completed (L79–89), though the document never explicitly stamps the Phase 1 exit gate.\\n- Phase 2 has a sealed advisory package, resumable review tooling, and one completed calibration (L3–5, L129–212, L244–287), but not its exit gate.\\n- Phase 3 is explicitly complete (L3, L403–407, L1505–1508).\\n- Phase 4 and Phase 5 have no completion claim.\\n\\nTwo plan-text inconsistencies are worth flagging:\\n\\n- The older reconciliation section says different-ID facts are cross-linked and queued as proposals (L1043–1058), while the current status/rollout says candidate mode keeps them separate and does not use executable proposals (L37–51, L1496–1499). The latter appears authoritative.\\n- The open-questions footer says the questions at L1583–1597 block broader automation/default promotion (L1599–1601), but paraphrase merging is elsewhere explicitly optional with an exact-only fallback. Those questions should be triaged into true default blockers versus post-MVP research.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/rework_plan_agentic_gates\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08d05-9960-7203-b218-368eb24fc42b"}}}
