{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T20:44:13.001Z","ordinal":38455,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0873a68aa02aff8f016aa31691c6248198ab5afbd23daea96e","status":"completed","call_id":"call_gx1pJvjFM00WvCewaoJusFX4","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md\\n@@\\n performance, quality, and progress against the phase contract. Each is blind\\n-to the other verdicts and prior acceptance. A unanimous valid verdict passes or\\n-fails the gate. A valid two-to-one verdict is decisive unless the dissent marks\\n-a critical safety, privacy, authority, or source-faithfulness concern. Any\\n-other split, unavailable judge, malformed response, or critical dissent is an\\n-escalation: Codex Astra receives the sealed evidence, rubric, all available\\n-primary verdicts, and their bounded rationales, then records one digest-bound\\n-escalation judgment of pass, fail, or insufficient-evidence. Astra is a tie\\n-breaker and escalation judge, never a fourth routine vote and never a substitute\\n-for missing evidence.\\n+to the other verdicts and prior acceptance. Three matching valid verdicts, a\\n+valid two-to-one majority, or two matching valid verdicts when the third judge\\n+is unavailable are decisive unless a dissent marks a critical safety, privacy,\\n+authority, or source-faithfulness concern. A split without a majority or a\\n+critical dissent invokes Codex Astra: Astra receives the sealed evidence,\\n+rubric, all available primary verdicts, and their bounded rationales, then\\n+records one digest-bound tie-break judgment of pass, fail, or\\n+insufficient-evidence. Fewer than two valid primary verdicts fails closed.\\n+Astra is never a fourth routine vote or a substitute for missing coverage.\\n@@\\n-the delivery-and-acceptance policy: valid unanimity, or a non-critical valid\\n-two-to-one result, is decisive; critical dissent, an invalid/missing judge, or\\n-a non-decisive split invokes Codex Astra once as the escalation judge. Astra\\n-receives the sealed evidence, rubric, all available primary verdicts, and their\\n-bounded rationales, then records one digest-bound pass, fail, or\\n-insufficient-evidence judgment. Insufficient evidence leaves the gate open; it\\n-cannot fabricate a label or compensate for missing coverage.\\n+the delivery-and-acceptance policy: matching valid verdicts or a non-critical\\n+valid two-to-one result are decisive. A split without a majority or a critical\\n+dissent invokes Codex Astra once. Fewer than two valid primary verdicts fails\\n+closed without asking Astra to replace missing coverage. Astra receives the\\n+sealed evidence, rubric, all available primary verdicts, and their bounded\\n+rationales, then records one digest-bound pass, fail, or insufficient-evidence\\n+judgment. Insufficient evidence leaves the gate open; it cannot fabricate a\\n+label or compensate for missing coverage.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08d05-9960-7203-b218-368eb24fc42b"}}}
