{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T20:44:25.910Z","ordinal":38465,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a08d10-87b6-7952-a8f3-11b76e964adb","call_id":"call_lX8y78db6lBkpnYTwoSkm9gN","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"16:delegated to a cheaper Sol, Terra, or Luna subagent with explicit file/module\n22:Every Phase 0–4 acceptance gate is independently scored from the same sealed,\n23:redacted evidence digest by Claude, Copilot, and Cursor. Each judge reports\n29:critical dissent invokes Codex Astra: Astra receives the sealed evidence,\n45:final Phase 5 human recomputation and approval.\n196:dissent invokes Codex Astra once. Fewer than two valid primary verdicts fails\n204:for the final Phase 5 human audit. It is not run in Phases 0–4 and no additional\n215:above. The final Phase 5 human audit recomputes the same metrics and is the\n538:- Preserve at least 98 percent candidate recall for explicit user standing\n539:  rules, preferences, and closed negatives, and at least 95 percent candidate\n541:  extraction agent runs; confirm both in the final Phase 5 human audit.\n555:- Reduce input tokens by 85-95 percent and total agent calls by at least 90\n962:extraction calls instead of 579 at 64 KiB, about 90 percent fewer. Cross-session\n1394:without the corresponding evidence digest. Claude, Copilot, and Cursor score\n1396:against the same rubric. Codex Astra is called only for the defined escalation\n1408:- At least 98 percent span recall for explicit human standing rules,\n1410:- At least 95 percent span recall across all sealed-evaluation durable facts.\n1416:- The sealed, stratified 500-exchange filtered-out agentic audit finds no\n1449:  two-percentage-point margin and has higher or equal durable precision.\n1463:paired evaluation supports it; the final Phase 5 human recomputation must then\n1469:- no more than a two-percentage-point absolute recall loss against legacy\n1479:- at least 80 percent fewer extraction calls than 64 KiB legacy mode;\n1480:- at least 90 percent fewer total agent calls than the extraction-plus-reconcile\n1482:- at least 85 percent fewer provider input tokens;\n1507:  run to a Sol, Terra, or Luna implementation subagent.\n1523:  and purge integration to bounded Sol, Terra, or Luna work items.\n1539:  results, split retry, and usage accounting to bounded Sol, Terra, or Luna\n1552:  Sol, Terra, or Luna work items.\n1575:  reuse to bounded Sol, Terra, or Luna work items.\n1663:- Claude, Copilot, and Cursor are independent provisional gate judges; Codex\n M docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md\n docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md | 450 ++++++++++++++++++++++--------------\n 1 file changed, 273 insertions(+), 177 deletions(-)\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08d05-9960-7203-b218-368eb24fc42b"}}}
