{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T20:45:35.874Z","ordinal":38498,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0200a-63d8-7b21-adef-c3850aecebf7","turn_id":"01a08d05-9960-7203-b218-368eb24fc42b","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0873a68aa02aff8f016aa316eb86a88198a2c63fd8d80397b1","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Reworked and pushed as `9cef13a5`.\n\nThe [candidate distillation plan](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md) now specifies:\n\n- Sol, Terra, and Luna subagents own bounded implementation tasks.\n- The main agent orchestrates, integrates, and judges performance, quality, and plan progress.\n- Claude, Copilot, and Cursor independently score every Phase 0–4 gate.\n- Codex Astra is used only when the primary panel lacks a decisive result or has a critical dissent.\n- Human scoring occurs only once, in Phase 5, as the final default-promotion gate.\n- Humans receive all available judge scores and concise rationales in bounded resumable batches.\n- Human rejection creates one consolidated remediation slice and delta-only reevaluation—not an open-ended tuning loop.\n- The original quantitative thresholds remain unchanged.\n- Safe paraphrase merging and relationship consumers are explicitly optional research.\n\nThe historical 20-item calibration remains documented but is no longer an intermediate gate. Both remotes point to the new commit."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1789073131539,"completed_at_ms":1789073135874}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T20:45:35.879Z","ordinal":38499,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0873a68aa02aff8f016aa316eb86a88198a2c63fd8d80397b1","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Reworked and pushed as `9cef13a5`.\n\nThe [candidate distillation plan](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md) now specifies:\n\n- Sol, Terra, and Luna subagents own bounded implementation tasks.\n- The main agent orchestrates, integrates, and judges performance, quality, and plan progress.\n- Claude, Copilot, and Cursor independently score every Phase 0–4 gate.\n- Codex Astra is used only when the primary panel lacks a decisive result or has a critical dissent.\n- Human scoring occurs only once, in Phase 5, as the final default-promotion gate.\n- Humans receive all available judge scores and concise rationales in bounded resumable batches.\n- Human rejection creates one consolidated remediation slice and delta-only reevaluation—not an open-ended tuning loop.\n- The original quantitative thresholds remain unchanged.\n- Safe paraphrase merging and relationship consumers are explicitly optional research.\n\nThe historical 20-item calibration remains documented but is no longer an intermediate gate. Both remotes point to the new commit."}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08d05-9960-7203-b218-368eb24fc42b"}}}
